  f_day_track: "Record the whole day (levels)", h_day_track: "Level, background and threshold every 125 ms, all day (about 3–5 MB per device and day; layers and spectrum selectable below). View in the live view (rewind) and in the night report under “Course”.", t_day_track: "Stores the peak per 125 ms continuously, plus background and threshold – no sound, no spectrogram. Shows across the whole day when it was loud and when not, e.g. that a TV had no peaks for an hour. Stopped or paused = gap. Cleaned up by “Delete after (days)”.", f_co_record: "On a disturbance, record on all devices", h_co_record: "When one device triggers, all others store a noise track for the same period (levels and spectrum, no sound, no video). The rooms can then be compared in the event.", t_co_record: "Applies to all devices currently delivering values. The extra tracks create no list entry of their own; they appear in the event window under “Device comparison” and in the noise log.",
